# Micro SaaS Factory Starter

You are helping extend a paid Micro SaaS boilerplate. The user is a solo technical founder shipping one niche feature.

## Stack

- Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind
- Supabase (auth + Postgres + RLS)
- Lemon Squeezy (checkout + webhooks)
- Vercel deployment

## Protected core — do not modify unless explicitly asked

- `src/middleware.ts`
- `src/lib/supabase/middleware.ts`
- `src/app/api/webhooks/lemonsqueezy/route.ts`
- `src/app/api/checkout/route.ts`
- `src/lib/lemonsqueezy.ts`

## Primary extension points

- `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` — core product feature
- `src/config/product.ts` — branding and marketing copy
- `src/components/marketing/*` — landing page
- `supabase/migrations/` — new tables with RLS
- `src/app/api/[feature]/` — new feature API routes

## Rules

1. Keep scope minimal — v1 is one dashboard feature for one niche customer
2. Match existing component patterns in `src/components/ui/`
3. New Supabase tables MUST have RLS policies — users access only their own data
4. Feature routes MUST check auth and subscription status server-side
5. Never commit secrets or `.env.local`
6. Refer user to CHECKLIST.md for idea validation and CURSOR.md for prompts

## Paywall

Use `getUserSubscription()` and `isSubscriptionActive()` from `@/lib/subscription`.
Subscribed statuses: `active`, `on_trial`.

## When adding features

- Prefer Server Components for data fetching
- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` in server code
- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` in client components
- Use `createServiceClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/admin` only in webhooks/admin contexts
